hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24145","Abd al-Rahman and Bahz said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, Bahz said, Abu Imran al-Jawni informed us, from Alqamah ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Maqil ibn Yasar, that Umar employed al-Numan ibn Muqarrin, then he mentioned the hadith. He said, meaning al-Numan: But I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when he did not fight at the beginning of the day he delayed fighting until the sun declines and winds blow and victory descends."
"24146","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from al-Numan ibn Muqarrin, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and a man insulted a man with him. He said: The insulted man began saying: Upon you be peace. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed an angel between you defends you; whenever this one insults you he says to him: Rather you, and you are more deserving of it. When he says to him: Upon you be peace, he says: No, rather to you, you are more deserving of it."
"24147","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb, meaning Ibn Shaddad, narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from al-Numan ibn Muqarrin, he said: We came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among four hundred of Muzaynah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us with his command. Some of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, we have no food to take as provision. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Umar: Provision them. He said: I have only a remainder of dates, and I do not see it availing them anything. He said: Go and provision them. He took us to an upper room of his, and in it were dates like the white young camel. He said: Take. The people took their need. He said: I was at the last of the people. He said: I turned and did not miss the place of a date, though four hundred men had carried from it."
